## Goal
DEV-47: harden the ask panel in portero against accidental or spoofed approvals. Add a short key guard after the panel appears, sanitize the title and Remember paths, and bound the ask queue.

## Problems
The session slice shows only the final cross-review step, which found no actionable bugs. Tests could not be run in the review sandbox because Go could not create its build directory (read-only environment). No other problems appear in the slice.

## Decision
Based on the commit message and changed files:
- `internal/handler/panel.m`: ignore key input for 400 ms after the panel appears, so keystrokes meant for another window cannot answer the prompt.
- `internal/rules/remember.go`: strip Unicode format and separator characters from the title and Remember paths, so the displayed text cannot be spoofed with invisible or look-alike characters and a saved rule matches what the user saw.
- `cmd/portero/app.go`: cap the ask queue at 50 so a flood of requests cannot grow it without limit.
- Tests added in `cmd/portero/ask_test.go` and `internal/rules/rules_test.go`.

A cross-review with Codex against origin/main was run and recorded as done for DEV-47.

